From: Christian Andrej Görlach <cgoerlac@gmail.com>
Subject: [SRU][N][PATCH 1/1] UBUNTU: SAUCE: io_uring/kbuf: fix inverted reserved-field checks

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2162843

The Noble backport of "io_uring/kbuf: use mem_is_zero()" replaced
mem_is_zero() with memchr_inv() but kept the negation. The helpers have
opposite results for an all-zero area.

This rejects valid buffer-ring registration, unregistration and status
requests with EINVAL, and accepts requests with nonzero reserved bytes.

Remove the three negations to restore the original checks. Allocation
and ring lifetime handling stay unchanged.

The same correction is already in Ubuntu-bluefield-6.8.0-1035.40.
Its corrected kbuf.c matches the Noble file with these three changes.

Signed-off-by: Christian Andrej Görlach <cgoerlac@gmail.com>
---
 io_uring/kbuf.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/io_uring/kbuf.c b/io_uring/kbuf.c
--- a/io_uring/kbuf.c
+++ b/io_uring/kbuf.c
@@ -549,7 +549,7 @@
 
 	if (copy_from_user(&reg, arg, sizeof(reg)))
 		return -EFAULT;
-	if (!memchr_inv(reg.resv, 0, sizeof(reg.resv)))
+	if (memchr_inv(reg.resv, 0, sizeof(reg.resv)))
 		return -EINVAL;
 	if (reg.flags & ~IOU_PBUF_RING_MMAP)
 		return -EINVAL;
@@ -608,7 +608,7 @@
 
 	if (copy_from_user(&reg, arg, sizeof(reg)))
 		return -EFAULT;
-	if (!memchr_inv(reg.resv, 0, sizeof(reg.resv)) || reg.flags)
+	if (memchr_inv(reg.resv, 0, sizeof(reg.resv)) || reg.flags)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	bl = io_buffer_get_list(ctx, reg.bgid);
@@ -629,7 +629,7 @@
 
 	if (copy_from_user(&buf_status, arg, sizeof(buf_status)))
 		return -EFAULT;
-	if (!memchr_inv(buf_status.resv, 0, sizeof(buf_status.resv)))
+	if (memchr_inv(buf_status.resv, 0, sizeof(buf_status.resv)))
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	bl = io_buffer_get_list(ctx, buf_status.buf_group);
